      "id": "p1",
      "text": "When the Colorado Avalanche's core crumbled, losing the fallen star and the silenced leader to injuries, the rebel commander John Tortorella was installed. The old guard was overthrown, and the new regime imposed its will, guiding a 7-0-1 close and playoff runs. This desperate gamble, however, was not enough against the system's beneficiaries. The favored franchise executed clinically, sealing the inevitable sweep. The establishment advanced to the Stanley Cup Final, while the hopefuls fell short in four brutal games.",
